{
  "id": "mass_vs_weight",
  "title": "Mass vs Weight",
  "description": "Calculate the relationship between mass and weight using Newton's Second Law. Convert between SI units (kg, N), British Gravitational units (slugs, lbf), and English Engineering units (lbm, lbf).",
  "type": "chart-table",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "id": "mass_weight_calculator",
      "content": "## Mass and Weight Calculator\n\nUse Newton's Second Law (F = m × a) to calculate weight from mass:\n\n**Weight Formula:** Fg = m × ag\n\nWhere:\n- Fg = gravitational force (weight)\n- m = mass\n- ag = acceleration of gravity",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "mass_kg",
          "label": "Mass",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 1,
          "unit": "kg"
        },
        {
          "id": "gravity",
          "label": "Acceleration of Gravity",
          "type": "select",
          "defaultValue": "9.807",
          "options": [
            {
              "label": "Earth (SI) - 9.807 m/s²",
              "value": 9.807
            },
            {
              "label": "Earth (Imperial) - 32.174 ft/s²",
              "value": 32.174
            },
            {
              "label": "Moon - 1.62 m/s²",
              "value": 1.62
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "weight_N",
          "label": "Weight (SI Units)",
          "formula": "inputs.mass_kg * inputs.gravity",
          "unit": "N",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "weight_kN",
          "label": "Weight (SI - Kilonewtons)",
          "formula": "(inputs.mass_kg * inputs.gravity) / 1000",
          "unit": "kN",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "datatable",
      "id": "unit_systems_table",
      "content": "## Unit Systems Comparison",
      "headers": [
        "System",
        "Mass Unit",
        "Force/Weight Unit",
        "Gravity Constant",
        "Base Formula"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "SI (International System)",
